      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::009::nanostructural_characterization"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti substitution decreases dislocation-motion energy barriers, including cross-slip barriers.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti-induced distortions produce predominantly homogeneous, highly mobile dislocation flow.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "CoCrFeNiTi undergoes minimal dislocation pile-up and lock formation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "High dislocation mobility gives CoCrFeNiTi favorable plasticity but low strain hardening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Facile dislocation glide and low strain hardening are the primary causes of the alloy's low hardness and strength.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "CoCrFeNiTi has lower hardness and yield strength than a similarly processed CoCrFeNi baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "CoCrFeNi has less pronounced lattice distortion than CoCrFeNiTi.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The lower lattice distortion in CoCrFeNi produces more dislocation interactions and marginally higher hardness and strength.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
